  bk-pv-out : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Real approximate -> [Device] Integer
  bk-pv-out (yb) (heads) (sq) (d) (h) (row) (col) (v) =
    if row < sq then (if col < d then device-store-approx yb ((row * heads + h) * d + col) v else 0) else 0

 Attention in one launch for the rows of one head, the scores never
 written: a workgroup takes 64 query rows and walks the keys 64 at a time,
 keeping each row's running max and exponent sum (online softmax) and 64 x d
 outputs, 2 rows x 5 columns a thread, so d is at most 40. Per key tile the
 scores are bk-attn-4x4's tile in 16-wide steps of d; the row max and sum
 reduce through words 2080 to 3103 (16 per row); the running max, sum and
 rescale factor sit at words 3104, 3168 and 3232; p and v go through words 0
 and 1040 a quarter of the tile (16 keys) at a time. One function carries
 every loop, because WGSL has no recursion and the plug makes a loop of a
 self tail call only; q < 0 is the score phase, q 0 to 3 the quarter, jj the
 key within it (-1 to stage it), and every branch around a barrier reads
 only uniform counters.

